<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niksar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Neocaesarea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niksar is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokat">Tokat</a> Province, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, on the Kelkit river. As ancient Neocaesarea it was a city of Pontus and the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> Gregory Thaumaturgus. In the late 11th century it fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danishmendids">Danishmendids</a>, for whom it was an early capital, and their mosques, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasa</a> and tombs survive in the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niksar.jpg" alt="Niksar" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bertramz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Niksar,KaleSW.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
